  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "XvAdS9EsYEakp00Gdn/hV2vN3nQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:25.737Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "adesso Group holds a unique position in the directory: it is the only firm Camunda-certified in all three DACH countries \u2014 Gold in Switzerland, Silver in Germany and Austria \u2014 and it also appears as a Flowable partner, making it dual across the two process-orchestration platforms the corpus tracks most closely.\n\nTri-country certification is not just breadth. It means the process-automation practice is organised as a group capability with certified staff in each national market, so the practice can carry a technology across borders instead of trialling it in one office. For a thesis that needs European reach, that is the most valuable structural fact in the cohort.\n\nWhat holds it at priority 3 is scale: 11,000-plus staff, which the record calls a committee sale. Above a certain size, a technology decision passes through alliance management and architecture review rather than a delivery lead, and the calendar for that process is measured in quarters. So the depth is real and the entry point is expensive \u2014 the same tension recorded for the separate adesso SE row, which is filed at priority 9 on scale with Camunda as its stack and no Flowable attribution. Two rows, one group, two tool attributions and two rankings: worth reconciling before either is acted on. Provenance is the Flowable Partner Finder mined on 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- adesso Group (CH Zurich + DE + AT) \u2014 adesso.ch\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> 11,000+ staff \u2014 committee sale. DUAL and the only firm Camunda-certified across all three DACH countries (Gold CH, Silver DE/AT) \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:25.737486Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:25.737491Z"
    }
  },
